<DocsLayout
  title="API contract"
  subtitle="packages/api is schemas and HttpApi groups. No handlers. No database. Parity is unfinished."
  description="CADCAMFUN HTTP contract: groups, errors, the generated client, and the 67 of 195 coverage."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="status" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Status</h2>
    <p>
      WP3 on the task board is <strong>in progress</strong> — 67/195 legacy route files are in
      the contract (<code>bun run --filter @cadcamfun/api coverage</code>). Owner directory:
      <code>packages/api</code> (<code>@cadcamfun/api</code>). Spec:
      <code>specs/05-api-sidecar.md</code>. The inventory of all 195 files is
      <code>specs/api-inventory.md</code>.
    </p>
    <DocCallout type="warn" title="Contract coverage is not handler coverage">
      <p>
        The coverage script measures the contract only. Declaring a route does not mean the
        sidecar serves it. Spec 05 says about 15% of the 195 legacy route files are served, and
        that handler parity needs its own HTTP tests. Families without a contract are still
        missing. See <code>specs/11-api-parity-brief.md</code>. Do not describe the API as
        finished parity.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

