  <section id="errors" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Errors and concurrency</h2>
    <p>
      Payloads are Schemas. Errors are <code>Schema.TaggedError</code> with HTTP status
      annotations.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Tag</th><th>Status</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>NotFound</code></td><td>404</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Validation</code></td><td>422</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Conflict</code></td><td>409</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Unauthorized</code></td><td>401</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Internal</code></td><td>500</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Collection endpoints take <code>?limit&amp;cursor&amp;q</code> with opaque cursors. Updates
      send <code>If-Match: &lt;updatedAt ISO&gt;</code>. A mismatch is <code>Conflict</code>.
      Drawing and toolpath JSON is validated by the WP1 and WP2 schemas, carries
      <code>schemaVersion</code>, and writes a version snapshot. Spec 05 caps snapshots at the 50
      most recent per entity.
    </p>
    <p>
      Streaming chat is Server-Sent Events. Typed events are <code>delta</code>,
      <code>tool_call</code>, <code>tool_result</code>, <code>done</code>, and <code>error</code>.
      Spec 08 also names <code>permission_request</code> on <code>AiEvent</code>. Stateless
      workflow endpoints (title, design analysis, machining parameters, G-code optimization,
      design suggestions) return advice and do not mutate drawings or operations.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every request needs <code>Authorization: Bearer</code> for the per-launch shell token.
      Auth routes may also send <code>x-session-token</code>. A valid session token selects that
      account. A missing, expired, or forged token falls back to the local profile. Auth
      <code>set-cookie</code> headers are optional in the contract because webview
      <code>fetch</code> hides them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="client" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Client</h2>
    <p>
      The desktop and tests construct <code>ApiClient.layer(&#123; baseUrl, token &#125;)</code>.
      Client middleware attaches the bearer token and does not persist it. After a contract
      change, regenerate both clients. Spec 05’s change log says generated files stay
      generator-owned.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="ts" title="Layer the UI provides once">
{`ApiClient.layer({
  baseUrl, // http://127.0.0.1:<port>
  token    // per-launch, from the Tauri command
})`}
    </DocCode>
    <p>
      Contract tests encode and decode every schema and serialise <code>Api</code> to an OpenAPI
      snapshot. <code>apps/sidecar/test/typed-client.test.ts</code> runs the generated client
      against real handlers, including multipart plugin install, so a drift fails a test.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="routes" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Core routes</h2>
    <p>
      Spec 05 §2’s table is the v6.0 minimum. The inventory wins where they differ. Paths below
      are the native contract. Legacy handlers often live under <code>/api/...</code> and the
      sidecar keeps those paths for parity.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Group</th><th>Examples</th><th>Tables</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>system</td><td><code>GET /health</code>, <code>GET /version</code>, legacy <code>GET /api/health</code></td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>projects, drawings, components</td><td>CRUD, versions</td><td><code>Project</code>, <code>Drawing</code>, <code>Component</code> and version tables</td></tr>
        <tr><td>toolpaths</td><td><code>POST /toolpaths/:id/generate</code>, <code>POST /toolpaths/:id/gcode</code>, <code>POST /api/toolpaths/verify</code></td><td><code>Toolpath</code>, <code>ToolpathVersion</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>library</td><td>materials, tools, machine configs, import/export JSON</td><td><code>Material</code>, <code>Tool</code>, <code>MachineConfig</code>, <code>LibraryItem</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>costs</td><td><code>POST /costs/estimate</code></td><td><code>CostSettings</code>, <code>ProductionCostEstimate</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>files</td><td><code>POST /files/import</code>, <code>POST /files/export</code></td><td><code>FileUpload</code> metadata; blobs under <code>&lt;dataDir&gt;/files/</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>ai</td><td><code>PUT /ai/credentials</code>, <code>POST /ai/chat</code> (SSE), <code>GET /api/ai/models</code></td><td><code>AIAnalysisLog</code>; context in <code>LocalKeyValue</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>plugins</td><td>list, install, enable, disable, config</td><td><code>PluginRegistryEntry</code>, <code>PluginConfiguration</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>vcs</td><td>status, commit, pulls, <code>POST …/actions/dispatch</code></td><td><code>GitRepo</code>, <code>GitObject</code>, <code>PullRequest</code>, <code>WorkflowRun</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      <code>GET /api/ai/models</code> accepts optional <code>configuredOnly</code>
      (<code>true</code> or <code>false</code>). The default remains the full list.
      <code>POST /api/toolpaths/manufacture</code> is a stateless kernel call: it takes a
      versioned CAD snapshot and returns NC plus evidence. It does not mutate a saved toolpath.
      G-code optimization proposals never write an operation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Stripe checkout is optional. Without <code>STRIPE_SECRET_KEY</code> the payment service
      fails with <code>PaymentError &#123; reason: "unconfigured" &#125;</code> and the routes
      keep their legacy 500 answers. There is no license-key path.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="boundaries" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Boundaries</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>packages/api</code> must not contain server handlers, a database client, or filesystem access.</li>
      <li>The UI must import this package for types and the client. It must not import <code>apps/sidecar</code>.</li>
      <li>Generated files under <code>client/generated</code> and <code>sdk/generated</code> must not be hand-edited.</li>
      <li>A new route family is not implemented until an in-process HTTP test calls the handler.</li>
      <li>Webhooks and cron routes that need a cloud signature stay behind an Effect service with a local default. They must keep the legacy HTTP shape.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section id="authorization" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Authorization</h2>
    <p>
      <code>Api</code> extends <code>HttpApi.make("cadcamfun")</code> in
      <code>packages/api/src/index.ts</code>. The middleware key is
      <code>cadcamfun/api/Authorization</code> in <code>packages/api/src/auth.ts</code>.
      <code>HealthGroup</code> is the only group without that middleware. Every other group uses it:
      <code>system</code>, <code>auth</code>, <code>waitlist</code>, <code>analytics</code>,
      <code>user</code>, <code>ai</code>, <code>mcp</code>, <code>billing</code>, <code>misc</code>,
      <code>kv</code>, <code>production-costs</code>, <code>plugins</code>, <code>files</code>,
      <code>organizations</code>, <code>notifications</code>, <code>projects</code>,
      <code>materials</code>, <code>materialsStorage</code>, <code>tools</code>,
      <code>toolsStorage</code>, <code>machineConfigs</code>, <code>machineConfigsStorage</code>,
      <code>drawings</code>, <code>components</code>, <code>toolpaths</code>,
      <code>toolpathExtras</code>, <code>toolpathGenerator</code>, <code>cadExact</code>,
      <code>library</code>, <code>projectToolpaths</code>, <code>vcs</code>, <code>events</code>,
      and <code>companion</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

